Subject: [PATCH] daynight: always-start stats worker + persist/record forced mode + derive boot running_mode; jsonapi: rebuild encoder on numeric stream-config change
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (branch stable)

Two independent reliability fixes on T23 / isp_bypass=true.

==== Part 1: day/night stats + forced mode (Config/DayNightWorker/IMPSystem/main) ====
 (A) AE/day-night telemetry read -1 for the whole process life when
     daynight.enabled=false, because the DayNightWorker (sole writer of those
     values) was only started when enabled. Fix: always start the worker;
     automatic switching stays gated on daynight.enabled inside the loop.
 (B) A forced mode did not survive reboot and the live mode was misreported.
     daynight.force_mode was not a persisted config key; the worker never tagged
     the live mode for a forced camera. Fix: register daynight.force_mode as a
     persisted string key; the worker RECORDS it at startup (current + live_mode,
     suppress auto-inference) WITHOUT apply_mode() on the live pipeline.
 (C) A forced color/mono mode did not take at boot (a late set_running_mode does
     not stick on this sensor). Fix: derive image.running_mode from
     daynight.force_mode BEFORE the early set_running_mode; drop the redundant,
     stall-prone end-of-init re-assert.
 The IR-CUT filter + IR LED at boot are handled by the rootfs boot init
 (S56ircut) reading the same daynight.force_mode -- single source of truth.

==== Part 2: encoder config changes apply without a stream freeze (JsonAPI) ====
 Changing a numeric encoder setting (bitrate, fps, resolution, gop, profile, qp,
 ...) via the JSON API (which the web UI / Home Assistant / prudyntctl all use)
 updated the in-memory config member but NEVER asked the pipeline to rebuild --
 only "mode" set global_restart_video. VideoWorker reads stream fields live while
 the IMP encoder was built once, so the new value left the encoder stale and the
 stream froze until a manual restart. Fix: in JsonAPI handle_stream, when an
 encoder-/framesource-defining field actually CHANGES, set global_restart_video
 (and global_restart_rtsp for codec/format, resolution, and stream enable, which
 also rebuild the RTP sink). The dispatcher already notifies global_cv_worker_restart
 once after processing, so the existing, proven main-loop teardown+rebuild runs.
 Flags are set only on a real value change, so re-sending an unchanged value is a
 no-op (no needless restart). This is the targeted root-cause fix for the
 config-change freeze on every API-based control path.

Verified to apply cleanly to the pinned commit (git apply -p1 and patch -p1).

